        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "Calculation of Binding Energy per Nucleon"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "n9emmh4w7542q1t",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The iron nuclide "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                    "src": "{}_{26}^{56}\\mathrm{Fe}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " lies near the top of the binding energy curve (shown above) and is one of the most stable nuclides. What is the binding energy per nucleon (in MeV) for the nuclide "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                    "src": "{}_{26}^{56}\\mathrm{Fe}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (atomic mass of 55.9349 amu)?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "e1j8rb7fl7coljw",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "As in the previous example, we first determine the mass defect of the nuclide—which is the difference between the mass of 26 protons, 30 neutrons, and 26 electrons—and the observed mass of a "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                    "src": "{}_{26}^{56}\\mathrm{Fe}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " atom:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "35gpm1c3ajmp1sx",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "ogqjc7ogk1gokj8",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1xgmn73oz4gysqv",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{Mass}\\;\\mathrm{defect}\\;=\\;\\mathrm{Mass}\\;\\mathrm{of}\\;\\mathrm{subatomic}\\;\\mathrm{particles}\\;-\\;\\mathrm{mass}\\;\\mathrm{of}\\;\\mathrm{atom}\\\\=\\;\\left[(26\\times1.0073\\;\\mathrm{amu})\\;+\\;(30\\times1.0087\\;\\mathrm{amu})\\;+\\:(26\\times0.00055\\;\\mathrm{amu})\\right]\\;-\\;55.9349\\;\\mathrm{amu}\\\\=\\;56.4651\\;\\mathrm{amu}\\;-\\;55.9349\\;\\mathrm{amu}\\\\=\\;0.5302\\;\\mathrm{amu}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We next calculate the binding energy for one nucleus from the mass defect using the mass–energy equivalence equation:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "bmppm0bh5ys6gln",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "csbemnrfjft5nhf",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xaattznpbcrtt7n",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "E\\;=\\;mc^2\\;\\\\=\\;0.5302\\;\\mathrm{amu}\\left(\\frac{1.6605\\;\\times\\;10^{-27}\\;\\mathrm{kg}}{1\\;\\mathrm{amu}}\\right){(2.998\\;\\times\\;10^8\\;\\mathrm m/\\mathrm s)}^2\\\\=\\;7.913\\;\\times\\;10^{-11}\\;\\mathrm{kg}\\cdot\\mathrm m/\\mathrm s^2\\\\=\\;7.913\\;\\times\\;10^{-11}\\;\\mathrm J",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We then convert the binding energy in joules per nucleus into units of MeV per nuclide:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ga8mmkkoetv1yyp",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "pxn2e50x20wctjh",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "73gdwjtv6w8x1o0",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "7.913\\times10^{-11}\\;\\mathrm J\\;\\left(\\frac{1\\;\\mathrm{MeV}}{1.602\\times10^{-13}\\;\\mathrm J}\\right)\\;=\\;493.9\\;\\mathrm{MeV}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Finally, we determine the binding energy per nucleon by dividing the total nuclear binding energy by the number of nucleons in the atom:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "tem2581i96v7jqv",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "9w6fws0e3c59k6v",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ef7dgbhfyuaaf03",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{Binding}\\;\\mathrm{energy}\\;\\mathrm{per}\\;\\mathrm{nucleon}\\;=\\;\\frac{493.9\\;\\mathrm{MeV}}{56}\\;=\\;8.820\\;\\mathrm M\\mathrm e\\mathrm V/\\mathrm n\\mathrm u\\mathrm c\\mathrm l\\mathrm e\\mathrm o\\mathrm n",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that this value is almost 25% larger than the binding energy per nucleon for "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                    "src": "{}_2^4\\mathrm{He}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "5xcqk7ldnclyzue",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "(Note also that we used the same process as in an earlier example but with the additional step of dividing the total nuclear binding energy by the number of nucleons.)"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xnhrp3131u49w62",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
